### FancyChoice Backend - API Test File
### Base URL + tokens. Replace @token, @planId, @subscriptionId, @deliveryId, @paymentId after each step.
### VS Code: install "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = YOUR_JWT_HERE
@planId = YOUR_PLAN_ID_HERE
@subscriptionId = YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_ID_HERE
@deliveryId = YOUR_DELIVERY_ID_HERE
@paymentId = YOUR_PAYMENT_ID_HERE
@addressId = YOUR_ADDRESS_ID_HERE

### ── 0. Health check ─────────────────────────────
### GET /health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ── 1. AUTH ─────────────────────────────────────

### 1a. Send OTP (customer login/signup via phone)
### Use case: customer enters phone on Login screen -> Send OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "purpose": "login"
}

### 1b. Verify OTP + login (dev mode: OTP_BYPASS=true accepts any 6-digit, real OTP logged in backend console)
### Use case: customer enters OTP -> logged in, copy "token" into @token above
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 1c. Signup with password (new customer with address)
### Use case: Signup screen -> create account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Anish Patil",
  "phone": "9876543211",
  "email": "anish@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "address": {
    "label": "Home",
    "street": "Flat 101, MG Road",
    "city": "Pune",
    "state": "Maharashtra",
    "pincode": "411001",
    "instructions": "Call on arrival"
  }
}

### 1d. Login with password (phone or email + password)
### Use case: Login screen -> password tab
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "9876543211",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 1e. Get logged-in user (needs @token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1f. Logout (stateless - client discards token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── 2. USER / PROFILE ───────────────────────────

### 2a. Get profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2b. Update profile (name, delivery slots, notes)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Anish P",
  "deliveryPreferences": {
    "slots": ["morning", "evening"],
    "notes": "Less spicy, extra ghee"
  }
}

### 2c. Add address
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/address
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Office",
  "street": "Office 202, Hinjewadi Phase 1",
  "city": "Pune",
  "state": "Maharashtra",
  "pincode": "411057",
  "isDefault": false
}

### 2d. Update address (set as default)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/address/{{addressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isDefault": true,
  "instructions": "Gate 2, security will guide"
}

### 2e. Delete address
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/address/{{addressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── 3. PLANS ────────────────────────────────────

### 3a. List plans (public - Plans tab)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans

### 3b. Alias used by mobile app
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/plans

### 3c. Get single plan by slug or id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/2-rotis

### 3d. Create plan (admin only - login as admin 9999999999 first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "4 Rotis / Day",
  "slug": "4-rotis",
  "rotisPerDay": 4,
  "description": "For couples",
  "prices": { "monthly": 1599, "quarterly": 4299, "yearly": 15999 },
  "features": ["4 fresh rotis daily", "Pause anytime"],
  "sortOrder": 4
}

### 3e. Update plan (admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prices": { "monthly": 1099, "quarterly": 2999, "yearly": 10999 }
}

### 3f. Deactivate plan (admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/plans/{{planId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── 4. SUBSCRIPTIONS ────────────────────────────

### 4a. Create subscription (customer picks plan -> checkout)
### Copy a real _id from GET /api/plans into @planId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/create
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "planId": "{{planId}}",
  "billingCycle": "monthly",
  "deliverySlots": ["morning"],
  "autoRenew": true,
  "deliveryAddress": {
    "label": "Home",
    "street": "Flat 101, MG Road",
    "city": "Pune",
    "state": "Maharashtra",
    "pincode": "411001",
    "instructions": "Morning 7-9 AM"
  }
}

### 4b. Get my active subscription (Home screen)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/my-subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4c. Get my subscriptions (history, paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/my?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4d. Get subscription by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4e. Update subscription (change slots / address / auto-renew)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deliverySlots": ["morning", "evening"],
  "autoRenew": false,
  "deliveryAddress": {
    "label": "Home",
    "street": "Flat 101, MG Road",
    "city": "Pune",
    "state": "Maharashtra",
    "pincode": "411001"
  }
}

### 4f. Pause subscription (going on vacation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/pause
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Out of town for a week"
}

### 4g. Resume subscription
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4h. Cancel subscription
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── 5. DELIVERIES ───────────────────────────────

### 5a. Today's deliveries (customer: mine | deliveryBoy: assigned | admin: all)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/today
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5b. Delivery history (paginated, optional ?status=delivered)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/history?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5c. Get delivery by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5d. Get QR code for delivery (customer shows to delivery boy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/qr-code
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5e. Verify QR code (delivery boy scans)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/verify-qr
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_5d"
}

### 5f. Rate delivery (customer, only after delivered)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/rate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "score": 5,
  "comment": "Fresh and on time!"
}

### 5g. Update delivery status (deliveryBoy / admin only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "out_for_delivery",
  "lat": 18.5204,
  "lng": 73.8567
}

### 5h. Mark delivered (deliveryBoy / admin)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

### 5i. Assign delivery boy (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "deliveryBoyId": "PASTE_DELIVERY_BOY_USER_ID"
}

### ── 6. PAYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────

### 6a. Create payment intent (checkout - Stripe or mock if no keys)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/intent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subscriptionId": "{{subscriptionId}}",
  "currency": "INR"
}

### 6b. Create intent with direct amount (no subscription yet)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/intent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 999,
  "currency": "INR",
  "billingCycle": "monthly"
}

### 6c. Confirm payment (mock success - flips status to succeeded)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "success": true
}

### 6d. My payments (Billing screen)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/my?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6e. Refund payment (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── 7. ADMIN ────────────────────────────────────
### Login as admin first: phone 9999999999 / password admin123 (after seed)

### 7a. Dashboard stats (users, active subs, revenue, delivery stats)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7b. List users (optional ?role=customer&search=anish)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── TEST FLOW (happy path order) ────────────────
### 1. GET /health
### 2. POST /api/auth/send-otp (9876543210) -> POST /api/auth/verify-otp -> save token
### 3. GET /api/plans -> save plan _id into @planId
### 4. POST /api/subscriptions/create -> save subscription _id
### 5. GET /api/subscriptions/my-subscription
### 6. GET /api/deliveries/today -> save delivery _id
### 7. GET /api/deliveries/:id/qr-code -> POST /api/deliveries/:id/verify-qr
### 8. PATCH /api/deliveries/:id/status (out_for_delivery -> delivered)
### 9. POST /api/deliveries/:id/rate
### 10. POST /api/payments/intent -> POST /api/payments/:id/confirm
